Package: weightedBernoulli
Type: Package
Title: Quantiles of Independent Weighted Bernoulli Sums
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Arun Kumar", "Kuchibhotla",
    email = "arunku@stat.cmu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes exact finite-distribution quantiles and conservative
    upper quantile bounds for sums of independent Bernoulli random variables
    with nonnegative weights and possibly unequal success probabilities.
    A single function recognizes binomial, repeated-class, rank, and lattice
    structure, uses exact meet-in-the-middle computation for at most 25 active
    summands by default, and otherwise returns the minimum of the applicable
    numerical and concentration bounds within documented work limits. Methods
    include upward grid rounding, binomial count aggregation, conditional
    moment and moment-generating-function bounds, and Gaussian and binomial
    comparisons. See Bentkus and Dzindzalieta (2015) <doi:10.3150/14-BEJ603>,
    Pinelis (2012) <doi:10.1214/EJP.v17-2026>, and Montgomery-Smith (1990)
    <doi:10.1090/S0002-9939-1990-1013975-0>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    stats,
    utils
NeedsCompilation: no
